From decae3a3359940c04626e8a8ae52786af8875eb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <203348624+yaegerbomb42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:20:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop-proxy): harden compression, backpressure and
 frame masking

- Never negotiate permessage-deflate: stop forwarding the browser's
  sec-websocket-extensions upstream and stop echoing the upstream's
  extension header in the 101 reply, since the bridge re-frames every
  message.
- Apply slow-viewer backpressure: pause the upstream socket above 8 MB
  of unacked browser data, resume on drain, and close with 1001 if still
  above 32 MB after 10 s.
- Enforce RFC 6455 mask direction per hop: an unmasked browser frame or a
  masked container frame is a protocol error, answered with close 1002
  before teardown.
---
